# Phase 6 with every guard off: a job as it was before. A start asks nobody,
# a file of the protected list is collected and landed unasked, sixty hours
# of an open agent hold nothing, and no gate turns anything down. The stuck
# detector, which comes switched on, is switched off here as the person may.
agent T1.1: edit .env.example | commit | write-result | report done "the keys are named" | hang
agent T2.1: hang
file brief.md: Target: the shop | Change: your part | Constraints: none | Ownership: your own files | Acceptance: the check passes
git
orch: init
human: set stuck.watch off
orch: run new "the shop"                            -> expect r1
task T1 "The keys" --name keys --owns .env.example --check "test -f .env.example" --brief brief.md
task T2 "The cart" --name cart --owns cart.txt --check "test -f cart.txt" --brief brief.md
orch: start T1 T2                                   -> expect "(T1.1)" "(T2.1)"
await: attempts T1.1 reported
orch: accept T1                                     -> expect "T1 is done, checked"
term-event working T2
clock +60h
orch: status --sweep --quiet
as-worker T2.1: hook gate
orch: stop T2
orch: task cancel T2
human: land --local                                 -> expect "merged into main"
assert: T1 status done; T2 status cancelled; no event lost; no event twice
